# GET /.well-known/autoconfig/mail/config-v1.1.xml — step 1: which host.
#
# Thunderbird's account setup fetches this URL on the address's domain
# (after the ISPDB and autoconfig.<domain>, before Exchange autodiscover
# and hostname guessing) and, given a parseable answer, fills in the
# server itself — the user types only the address and password. It does
# NOT consult RFC 6186 `_imaps._tcp` SRV records. Apple Mail uses neither.
#
# The IMAP server for paris@<host> is <host> itself (the head does not
# route by name; the front door serves every hostname), so the answer is
# built from the request's Host, minus any :port. 085 renders it.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.method == "GET" && @web.req.url.path == "/.well-known/autoconfig/mail/config-v1.1.xml"
  EMIT ._ac.host = &get(&split(@web.req.host, ":"), "0"),
       ._ac.req = true
